# Heightmap exports are large binaries; track deliberately with `git add -f`
terrain/*.raw
terrain/*.r16

# Capture output is regenerated by scripts/capture.py on every scene change.
# ** so per-biome subdirs (captures/alpine/...) are covered — schema.md only
# requires output_dir to resolve INSIDE captures/, and an untracked capture
# would mark every later run's git stamp -dirty.
captures/**/*.png
captures/**/*.jpg
!captures/.gitkeep

# capture.py's concurrency sentinel: pid, start time and camera list,
# written while a run is live and cleared on orderly exit. TRANSIENT RUN
# STATE, not work. Committing it would bake a permanent "a capture is
# running" lie into the repo, and leaving it untracked made the
# session-protocol stop hook fire on every single capture run --
# a gate that cries wolf every time is a gate you learn to wave through,
# which is precisely the gate you need working when the dirty path is
# real. Added 2026-08-09.
CAPTURE_IN_PROGRESS

# Trash is a staging area for removals, never history
_trash/*
!_trash/.gitkeep

# UE project (LandscapeLab) — generated and machine-local artifacts
LandscapeLab/DerivedDataCache/
LandscapeLab/Intermediate/
LandscapeLab/Saved/
LandscapeLab/Binaries/
*.sln

# C++ plugin build output. The SOURCE under Plugins/*/Source is tracked; the
# compiled DLL and UHT's generated headers are derived and rebuild in ~80 s.
LandscapeLab/Plugins/*/Binaries/
LandscapeLab/Plugins/*/Intermediate/

# push_heightmap's staging texture. NOT source data: it is re-imported
# from terrain/alpine_heightmap.png on every push (push_heightmap.py
# :1769-1775), so it carries nothing the 7.1 MB PNG already in this repo
# does not. As TC_HDR_F32 (RGBA32F) at 2017x2017 it is ~65 MB of
# regenerable binary.
#
# Ignored rather than trusted-not-to-be-saved: it sits DIRTY in the
# editor after every push, so it appears in the close-the-editor "save
# these?" prompt, and "Save All" is one click. This makes that click
# harmless instead of expensive. The other /Game/Debug assets are small
# and stay tracked deliberately.
LandscapeLab/Content/Debug/T_PushHeight_Source.uasset

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Source assets are large and vendor-supplied — not ours to version.
Free/
# RULING 4: but the DERIVED artefacts are. A manifest nobody can review
# in a diff defeats the point of generating it, and the cached Blender
# measurement is the provenance behind fir_tree_01's mesh_extent_m — if
# it is not tracked, the next session re-measures or, worse, re-guesses.
# Negations must re-open the directory first: a pattern ending in `/`
# excludes the directory itself, and git will not descend into an
# excluded directory to find un-ignored children.
!Free/
Free/*
!Free/manifest.json
!Free/_measured/
!Free/_measured/*.json

# resource_guard.py mutual-exclusion lock — runtime state, not source
.heavy-op.lock

# Asset intake staging — vendor sources extracted from Downloads.
# Large (GB-scale) and reproducible from the original zips, which are
# recorded in ASSETS.md with source and licence. The CATALOGUE is
# tracked; the pixels are not.
Free/_intake/
terrain/external_heightmaps/*.png
terrain/external_heightmaps/**/*.png

# ---- Fab-delivered native content (FAB-PLUGIN intake branch) ----
# 15.9 GB of vendor uassets delivered by the in-editor Fab window into
# named top-level Content folders. NOT committed: they are re-downloadable
# from the user's Fab library, and ASSETS.md carries the source, licence
# and real path, which is the reproducibility contract this repo uses for
# every vendor asset (same as Free/_intake/).
#
# THE LINE: SOURCE is ignored, DERIVATIVES are committed.
# Anything the pipeline CREATES on top of Fab content is pipeline output
# and MUST be committed -- it is not re-downloadable.
#
# Git cannot enforce that here: it will NOT re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so no !negation can rescue a derivative written
# inside one of these folders. Two rules close the gap, and
# scripts/check_fab_boundary.py enforces them:
#   1. NEVER AUTHOR INTO A FAB FOLDER. Derivatives go to a convention path
#      (/Game/Meshes/Materials/, /Game/Foliage/, ...), which is tracked.
#   2. An IN-PLACE MODIFICATION (Nanite, LOD, collision) is NOT a
#      committable derivative -- the bytes are ignored and re-download
#      reverts them. Express it as a REPLAYABLE RECIPE STEP instead.
#
# RECOVERY FOR THESE FILES IS RE-DOWNLOAD, NOT GIT. A tag cannot roll back
# what git does not track; checkpoints before bulk ops here must say so.
#
# If any of these is ever REFERENCED by a saved level, that reference must
# be recorded in ASSETS.md, because a fresh clone will not have the bytes.
LandscapeLab/Content/KiteDemo/
LandscapeLab/Content/DragonCave/
LandscapeLab/Content/Atlantis_Ruins/
LandscapeLab/Content/StampIt/
LandscapeLab/Content/Mannequin/
LandscapeLab/Content/ThirdPerson/
LandscapeLab/Content/ThirdPersonBP/
LandscapeLab/Content/Geometry/
LandscapeLab/*.pdf

# Scratch UE project, created 2026-08-05 and EMPTY (Content/ has zero files).
# 119 MB of its 125 MB is Intermediate build artifacts — derived data, never
# versioned. Its editor was holding 1.8 GB and was a SECOND remote-exec editor,
# which is the conduct-rule-7 hazard; closed 2026-08-06.
# Deliberately ignored, not committed. To reclaim the disk: move to _trash/.
MyProject/
.claude/hooks/_state/

# Scratch payloads for standing rule 3's `git commit -F <path>`. The message
# IS the commit once it lands, so a copy on disk is a derived record that can
# only drift from it (non-negotiable 24). Keep the directory for the workflow;
# do not version its contents.
commits/

# Claude Code machine-local settings. Per-machine, not project truth; the
# migration to the 5080 box produced a fresh one.
.claude/settings.local.json

# `LandscapeLab 5.8/` -- an 11 GB UNTRACKED DUPLICATE of the UE project,
# created 2026-08-10 21:33 when the project was opened directly from the
# migration staging folder. Its AlpineLab_v1.umap is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the
# tracked copy (sha256 a641588f...), as is M_AlpineLab; it differs only in
# generated files and in .uproject EngineAssociation.
#
# IGNORED, NOT RESOLVED. bootstrap.py:54-55 defines UE_PROJECT_ROOT as
# REPO_ROOT/"LandscapeLab", so this directory is invisible to the rule 7
# identity gate -- an editor opened against it would write work git never
# sees. Ignoring it closes only the OTHER hazard: that a `git add -A`
# sweeps 11 GB into the history, which has happened before on this repo
# with a stray hook-state file.
#
# AWAITING RYAN'S DECISION: delete it outside the repo, or keep it
# deliberately. Do not resolve it by committing it.
LandscapeLab 5.8/

# 8K terrain INTERMEDIATES — deterministic, so they are rebuilt rather than stored.
# Each is ~102 MB and neither is an artefact of record: alpine_8k.png is the
# ADOPTED terrain (hash-proven, LFS-tracked, committed) and is what every
# consumer reads. Regenerate these two with:
#   python scripts/resample_heightmap.py --input terrain/alpine_heightmap.png \
#          --output terrain/alpine_8k_base.png --size 8129 --go
#   python scripts/composite_stamps.py --recipe recipes/alpine_8k.json --allow-clamp
# The composite is seed-locked and replays bit-identical; the sidecar
# terrain/alpine_8k_stamped.png.stamps.json IS committed and records the hash.
terrain/alpine_8k_base.png
terrain/alpine_8k_stamped.png

# 8K talus deposit CACHE — 504 MB, deterministic, regenerated by the selector bake.
# The tool's own words: "Cache the routed deposit. It is deterministic and
# expensive ... saturation is a TUNING knob that must be judged against a
# render." Storing half a gigabyte of regenerable cache is poor value; alpine's
# 2017 equivalent is only 31 MB and stays tracked. Regenerate with:
#   python scripts/make_variant_map.py --recipe recipes/alpine_8k.json
# (~33 min, routing converges at 859 steps against the 2400 cap)
terrain/alpine_8k_talus_deposit.npy

# Fab vendor content — ignored from 2026-08-14, matching the KiteDemo precedent
# at line 107. Bulk-adding tree packs would otherwise put tens of GB of
# re-downloadable vendor content into LFS permanently, and that is not undoable
# without rewriting history. Already-tracked files (the 9 Megascans surfaces)
# are unaffected: gitignore does not untrack.
# ACCEPTED COST: gitignored vendor content vanishes if Fab pulls the asset.
# Same trade already accepted for KiteDemo's 272 files.
LandscapeLab/Content/Fab/

# AND THE PATH ASSUMPTION ABOVE WAS WRONG — measured 2026-08-14, mid-import.
# "Add to Project" on a Quixel Megaplants item does NOT write to Content/Fab/.
# The Norway Spruce pack's 138 assets went to Content/Megaplant_Library/, so
# the rule written the day before to prevent exactly this covered none of it.
# The destination is per-VENDOR-PIPELINE, not a single Fab root: Megascans
# surfaces land in Content/Fab/Megascans/, Megaplants in Megaplant_Library/.
# Whichever root a pack chooses, it is re-downloadable vendor content and the
# same reasoning applies. Added BEFORE the import finished writing, because
# after is the expensive half.
LandscapeLab/Content/Megaplant_Library/
LandscapeLab/Content/Megascans/

# THIRD INSTANCE OF THE SAME CLASS, same night. Content/Fab/ was a GUESS;
# Megaplant_Library/ was found mid-import; these five were found by checking
# BEFORE committing, which is the only reason they are here and not in LFS.
# Every Fab vendor pack invents its own top-level Content/ directory and there
# is no shared prefix to match on, so this list grows with every import and
# CANNOT be relied on to be complete. Check after every import:
#     git status --porcelain     (anything under LandscapeLab/Content/ is suspect)
# Sizes recorded so a future reader knows what was at stake: 3.5 GB across
# these five, against the 1.9 GB already covered above.
LandscapeLab/Content/GV_FreeShrubsPack/
LandscapeLab/Content/HighPoly_Tree_Model/
LandscapeLab/Content/PN_interactiveSpruceForest/
LandscapeLab/Content/PN_WildBerries/
LandscapeLab/Content/TreesGen02_01/

# Textures exported OUT of vendor packs for offline measurement. Derived from
# gitignored vendor content and re-derivable by re-running
# scripts/measure_tree_packs.py, so committing them would put vendor bytes
# into LFS through the back door (22.6 MB for the first two 4096s alone).
# The MEASUREMENTS are committed -- Free/_measured/tree_packs.json -- and they
# are what any later claim is checked against.
_verify/tex/

# Mechanically derived recipes: projections of a real recipe, regenerated on
