# The MetaHuman ASSEMBLE output, 2026-08-16: 252 uassets, 631 MB, written by
# pressing Assemble on MHC_AlpineHero. It holds the real assembled character
# -- BP_MHC_AlpineHero, SKM_MHC_AlpineHero_FaceMesh / _BodyMesh, PHYS, the
# baked head and body virtual textures, the Hair_M_Layered groom -- plus the
# shared /Game/MetaHumans/Common/ library.
#
# IGNORED, on the same rule as everything above: it is DERIVED, and its
# source (MHC_AlpineHero.uasset, 145 MB) is tracked. Regenerating it is one
# click, documented in RECIPES R-HEROFACE, and 631 MB of LFS for something a
# click rebuilds is a bad trade.
#
# THE ONE THING TO KNOW IF IT GOES MISSING: Assemble leaves all 252 packages
# DIRTY AND UNSAVED. The editor reports "MetaHuman Character assembly
# succeeded" and nothing is on disk until they are saved -- which is exactly
# how it looked like Assemble had done nothing on 2026-08-16.
LandscapeLab/Content/MetaHumans/

# THE WHOLE-RIG SCRATCH CHARACTER — deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# `MHC_AlpineHero_Scratch` exists to absorb a whole-rig import, whose cost is
# advertised as a PERMANENT per-asset body-type lock. It is expendable BY
# CONSTRUCTION, and it is re-derivable in one command from a TRACKED source:
# EditorAssetLibrary.duplicate_asset("/Game/Hero/MHC_AlpineHero", ...) —
# proven faithful at compare_face_state 0.001 when it was made. 145 MB of LFS
# for something a single call rebuilds is the same bad trade as the assembled
# MetaHumans above.
#
# THIS IS NOT THE Content/Hero/Generated MISTAKE. That regression lost meshes
# nothing could re-derive; this file's producer is a tracked asset plus one
# reflected call, both recorded in RECIPES R-HEROWHOLERIG.
LandscapeLab/Content/Hero/MHC_AlpineHero_Scratch.uasset

# ASSEMBLED (unpacked) MetaHuman output — derived, and re-derivable in one
# call. `build_meta_human` writes ~83 packages / 299 MB per character under
# Content/Hero/Unpacked/<CharacterName>/. The producer is the character asset
# plus MetaHumanCharacterEditorSubsystem.build_meta_human, both recorded in
# RECIPES R-HEROWHOLERIG, so this is the Content/MetaHumans trade again:
# 299 MB of LFS for something a single call rebuilds is a bad trade.
#
# THE ONE THING TO KNOW IF IT GOES MISSING: the assemble leaves every package
# DIRTY AND UNSAVED, and on 2026-08-19 the editor stopped answering remote
# execution immediately after the build TWICE — so the save must happen inside
# the SAME payload as the build, or the output dies with the process.
LandscapeLab/Content/Hero/Unpacked/

# BODY DIAGNOSTIC SCRATCH — expendable, re-derivable in one call from the
