*.blend1

# ---- groom chain per-stage intermediates and Alembic exports -------------
# The DiffLocks restyle chain is dl_L1 -> P1 -> p0 -> p3 -> p4 -> p5, and on
# 2026-08-23 six tuning arms of it were run (fa_ fb_ fc_ fd_ hg_ hh_ hi_ mn_)
# to chase the envelope. The FINAL blend of every arm that informed a ruling is
# TRACKED -- fb_FALL2, fe_FALL5, hi_HUG3, mn_MIN, dl_FLIP28, dl_FLIP28b -- and
# so is the shipped chain. What is ignored here is the PER-STAGE files inside
# an arm, each of which is one documented Blender command away from a tracked
# parent with its parameters recorded in the commit message.
#
# Being deliberate about which half is which is the point. This project's rule
# is that a derived artefact is tracked when it is PROVENANCE (Free/_measured
# above says so in as many words); a mid-chain blend is not provenance for
# anything, because the arm's finding lives in its final blend and its numbers.
#
# The .abc is the UE-side export: 55 MB, regenerated by one run of
# export_hero_groom.py from a tracked .blend, and its `.groomstats.json`
# sidecar -- which carries the widths, the root-UV census and the exporter
# SHA-256 that the draw gate checks -- IS tracked. The sidecar is the evidence;
# the geometry is a copy of the blend.
hero/groomloop/difflocks/*.abc
hero/groomloop/difflocks/f[a-d]_[Pp]*.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/f[a-e]_p[0-9].blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/fa_FALL.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/fc_FALL3.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/fd_FALL4.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/h[gh]_*.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/hi_[Pp]*.blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/hi_p[0-9].blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/mn_p[0-9].blend
hero/groomloop/difflocks/ff_p[0-9].blend

